    "created_at": "2026-11-03T10:27:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T10:27:32Z",
    "body": "Proposed design:\n\n```webidl\npartial dictionary MutationObserverInit {\n  sequence<DOMString> activeTemplateAttributeFilter;\n};\n\nenum MutationRecordActiveTemplateStatus { \"start\", \"update\", \"end\", \"abort\" };\n\npartial interface MutationRecord {\n  readonly attribute MutationRecordActiveTemplateStatus? activeTemplateStatus;\n  readonly attribute object? activeTemplateAttributes; // frozen, null-prototype\n};\n```\n\n```js\nnew MutationObserver(records => {\n  for (const r of records) {\n    if (r.activeTemplateStatus === \"abort\") showRetry(r.target, r.activeTemplateAttributes[\"data-request-id\"]);\n  }\n}).observe(document, { subtree: true, activeTemplateAttributeFilter: [\"data-request-id\"] });\n```\n\n- Passing `activeTemplateAttributeFilter` opts in and implies `childList: true`, the same way `attributeFilter` implies `attributes`. \n- `activeTemplateAttributes` is a snapshot of only the listed attributes when the patch starts. All records from one `<template for>` share the same object, so it can be used as a `WeakMap` key. \n- Records are queued per insertion, as today. Attribution is per record: a record has a non-null status only if the parser made that mutation for that `<template for>`. One record never mixes parser and script nodes. Nothing is held back while the network pauses (re @foolip's question).\n- `\"start\"` on a marker and empty patches produce `childList` records with no nodes. They go only to observers that opted in. This relaxes the \"addedNodes or removedNodes is non-empty\" assertion in \"queue a tree mutation record\" for those observers.\n- The parser inserts the `<template>` as an ordinary inert element, and that insertion is the `\"abort\"` record.\n- As far as nesting, each record carries the innermost `<template for>`'s attributes. `\"end\"` means that invocation's stream finished, not that nested includes have arrived.\n\nThe [explainer](https://github.com/WICG/declarative-partial-updates/blob/main/template-mutation-observer-explainer.md) contains walkthroughs (two chunks, a single-point marker, a missing target), the alternatives considered (new record types, events, exposing the element, a boolean option), and the security and privacy questionnaire.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
